CourseForum Technologies has introduced ProjectForum 3.0 and
CourseForum 3.0, major updates to its powerful but easy-to-use
web forum software for business and educational collaboration.

ProjectForum helps groups stay in constant communication, without the
endless meetings, expensive teleconferences, or the daunting costs and
complexity of other collaboration software packages.  CourseForum
brings greater interaction to online or face-to-face courses, helping
students to learn more effectively and saving time on routine questions.

Version 3.0 features two major new advancements, as well as a host of
smaller updates:

   * a brand new look, now also offering a choice of several different
     themes for each forum, and allowing custom themes to be easily
     created and added

   * new capabilities making it easier to integrate existing web
     information directly into forums, both standalone web pages and
     web services

The software is available for Mac OS X (including Panther),
Windows 98/ME/NT/2000/XP, Linux and FreeBSD.  ProjectForum licenses
are available starting from US$199, while CourseForum licenses start at
US$79.  Free versions of both products can also be downloaded, and a
hosting service is available.

For more information, to try our demo sites, or to download free or
evaluation versions, visit http://www.courseforum.com

